Sophie Casterwill used Breakspell to destroy the [[Gargoyle]] trap protecting the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]]. {{Source|Into the River of Secrets}}

Inside the [[Paris Catacombs]], Breakspell was used by Sophie alongside other spells to deactivate the [[Knights of Arc's Inner Circle]] protecting the [[Ring of Arc]], targeting every individual suit of armor. This left her exhausted afterwards. {{Source|Crawling the Catacombs}}

Sophie again used this spell to break a mystical laminate preventing [[Cypherdex]] from scanning a map of the inner maze of the [[Basilisk House]]. The laminate was set by [[DeFoe]] as a trap, predicting the Huntik team would attempt to scan the map. {{Source|Absent Heroes}}

[[Zhalia Moon]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] undid the petrifying effects of [[King Basilisk]] with this spell. {{source|Huntik.com|Huntik.com Webisodes}}

Breakspell was cast by Sophie Casterwill to break a magical barrier surrounding a ship sunk in the [[Stavropolous River]] initially thought to be the [[Argo]], allowing the Huntik team to explore it. {{Source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}}

Sophie once again used the spell counter the illusion of [[Cristine]], set by the [[Titans|Titan]] [[Madea]] to give Sophie fake books about her [[Casterwill family|family]]'s history. {{Source|The Beautiful Trap}}

This spell was cast by Sophie in order to open a chamber inside the [[Newgrange Passage Tomb]] containing the Titan [[Gybolg]]. As Sophie had noted when she used the spell, the door opened after a short time, trapping Lok on the outside of the room fighting [[The Organization|Organization]] [[Suits]]. She attempted to cast Breakspell again, but the seal was much stronger from the inside and the door couldn't be open. {{Source|Home Turf}}

Breakspell was unsuccessfully cast by Sophie Casterwill to attempt to break a powerful force barrier shielding a cave [[Lok Lambert]] had fallen into. The barrier was set ten years ago by [[Eathon Lambert]] to protect [[The Oracle]], residing in the cave. {{Source|The Unseen Guide}}

In an unofficial mission to confront [[Simon Judeau]] in his [[The Professor's castle|castle]], Sophie used the spell to destroy a cat-like anchor concealing the various traps guarding the entrance to the castle. [[The Professor]] also used Breakspell to break an illusion and reveal his true appearance to the Huntik team because of the [[Curse of the Legendary Titans]]. {{source|The Divine Comedy}} Sophie later cast Breakspell once again  in combination with Lok Lambert's [[Boltflare]] to break the Professor's ritual regarding the [[Amulet of Will]] and [[Behemoth]], [[Tao]] and [[Araknos]]. {{Source|The Mission}}

At one point, [[Zhalia Moon]] used the spell against a [[Suits|Suit]]. {{Source|TCG:SAS-104|SAS-104}}

As part of a plan to get inside [[Medusa's Cave]], Sophie used Breakspell to stop [[Kiel]] from casting one of his powers, helping [[Metagolem]] detain him. {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}}

Sophie used this spell once again against Kiel to stop one of his spells when fighting him by the entrance of the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]. {{Source|The Spiral War}}

In an elaborate plan to capture [[Rassimov]] by the [[Tomb of Tutankhamun]], Sophie cast Breakspell to prevent him from using one of his powers. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}}

After asking [[Cherit]] to give her all his power with his Energy Charge, Sophie Casterwill used Breakspell with [[Doublespell]] on the [[Spiral Mark]] in an attempt to stop the dark ritual sending the [[Red Comet]] to their location. However, the ritual was too strong and Sophie's efforts were in vain. {{Source|The Spiral Mark}}

{{Clear}}

